      "text": "Under the Labor Code, an employment is regular when the worker is hired to perform activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s ordinary business, except when the job is fixed for a specific project whose completion was determined at the time of engagement or when the work is seasonal and the employment lasts only for the season’s duration. If the work does not meet those conditions, it is deemed casual, and any employee who has rendered at least one year of service, continuous or broken, is thereafter considered regular with respect to that activity.",
