      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under Art. 100 of the Consumer Act, the supplier of a durable product is jointly liable for any quality imperfection that makes the product unfit for its intended use. If the defect is not fixed within thirty (30) days, the buyer may choose either a replacement of the same kind in perfect condition, an immediate refund of the purchase price with monetary updating, or a proportionate price reduction. The parties may agree to extend the correction period, but it cannot be shorter than seven (7) days nor longer than one hundred‑eighty (180) days. When the defect is so serious that repairing it would jeopardize the product’s quality, the buyer may use any of these alternatives immediately.",
      "evidence": [
