      "text": "Art. 68 of the Consumer Act requires that a warranty be enforced by presenting the warranty card or official receipt together with the product to the immediate seller; no other documents are needed. If the immediate seller is the manufacturer’s showroom or a distributor, the warranty must be honored right away. When the seller is a retailer that is not the distributor, the retailer must forward the claim to the distributor at no cost to the buyer and bears the expenses needed to satisfy the warranty if both the manufacturer and distributor fail to do so. The retailer’s liability is subsidiary and does not prevent it from later seeking reimbursement from the upstream parties.",
